      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose is over the maximum.\n\n**The problem:** 1700 mg three times daily adds up to **5100 mg/day**. The labeled maximum for metformin is **2550 mg/day** for immediate-release and **2000 mg/day** for extended-release. This order is about twice the immediate-release maximum. High doses raise the risk of lactic acidosis and serious GI side effects, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\n**This could be a mix-up between per-dose and daily amounts.** Did you mean one of these?\n\n1. **Metformin 850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals** (2550 mg/day, the immediate-release maximum)\n2. **Metformin 1700 mg total per day**, for example 850 mg twice daily with meals\n3. **Something else**, such as a different dose or the extended-release form. Let me know the regimen you want.\n\nPlease confirm the dose you want and I'll enter it. If you really do mean 1700 mg three times daily, please confirm that and give a clinical reason. I'll add it to the order note so pharmacy can review it."
      }
